<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John I of Castile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1358">1358</a>–1390</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> from 1379 to 1390, the son of Henry II and second king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-trastamara">House of Trastámara</a>. Married to Beatrice of Portugal, he claimed the Portuguese throne in 1383, but his army was defeated at Aljubarrota in 1385 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-of-portugal">John I of Portugal</a>. At home he reorganised the royal council and created the title Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> for the heir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-i-of-castile.jpg" alt="John I of Castile" width="299" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jaume Serra · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Juan_I)_Virgen_de_Tobed_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
